Lets define a few terms:

<> publicSet(X) for package X is a set comprising of all classes/interfaces that use the public modifier.

<> publicIndirectSet(X) for package X is a set comprising of all classes/interfaces used by public fields/methods in classes of
   publicSet(X).


<> When making a change use the following algorithm to figure out if the major version# of the different packages in your bundle
   need to change. A change can be any direct change to a class/interface within a bundle or an indirect change. An indirect
   change includes class/interfaces that are not backwards compatible in packages that have been upgraded to. Let all such changed
   classes be part of the set CHANGEDCLASSES.

   foreach public package (y) in Bundle (B) {
	foreach class (t) in CHANGEDCLASSES {
		if ((t is_a_member_of publicSet(y)) || (t is_a_member_of publicIndirectSet(y))) {
		   bump major version# of package y
		   break
		}
       	}
   }